  ["me2","F",2,"T","What does „Ich spiele oft Computerspiele“ mean?",["I often play computer games","I never play video games","I played computer games","I often buy computer games"],"The word oft means often, and spiele is present tense."],
  ["me2","F",2,"T","How do you say “My phone is broken”?",["Mein Handy ist kaputt","Mein Handy hat kaputt","Meine Handy ist kaputt","Mein Handy ist kaputten"],"The noun Handy is neuter (mein Handy), and an adjective after ist takes no ending."],
  ["me2","F",3,"G","Complete: Ich schicke ___ Bruder eine Nachricht.",["meinem","meinen","mein","meine"],"The person you send something to is the indirect object, in the dative: meinem Bruder."],
  ["me2","F",3,"T","Which is the correct translation of “I can’t live without my phone”?",["Ich kann ohne mein Handy nicht leben","Ich kann ohne meinem Handy nicht leben","Ich kann ohne mein Handy nicht lebe","Ich kann mit mein Handy nicht leben"],"The preposition ohne takes the accusative (mein Handy), and the infinitive leben goes to the end."],
  ["me2","F",4,"R","Read: „Meine Eltern sagen, ich spiele zu viel, aber ich mache immer meine Hausaufgaben zuerst.“ What do the parents think?",["The writer plays too much","The writer does no homework","The writer should play more","The games are too expensive"],"The parents say ich spiele zu viel: I play too much. The writer says homework always comes first."],
  ["me2","H",4,"T","What does „Ich bin süchtig nach meinem Handy“ mean?",["I am addicted to my phone","I am searching for my phone","I am sick of my phone","I am looking after my phone"],"The adjective süchtig means addicted; to search for is suchen nach."],
  ["me2","H",5,"G","Complete: Ich habe das neue Spiel gestern ___.",["heruntergeladen","geherunterladen","herunterladet","heruntergelädt"],"Separable verbs put ge- between the prefix and the stem in the perfect: herunter + ge + laden."],
  ["me2","H",5,"T","Which is the best translation of “I would buy a new laptop, but it costs too much”?",["Ich würde einen neuen Laptop kaufen, aber er kostet zu viel","Ich würde ein neuer Laptop kaufen, aber er kostet zu viel","Ich würde einen neuen Laptop kaufen, aber er kosten zu viel","Ich würde einen neuen Laptop gekauft, aber er kostet zu viel"],"The laptop is the object, so masculine Laptop needs einen neuen; würde takes an infinitive (kaufen) at the end."]
